# Feature Documentation Rule

When implementing or changing behavior for a feature, always create or update a feature doc in `docs/features/`.

## Goal

- Preserve implementation context so future agents and developers can safely modify the feature.
- Keep docs close to the code lifecycle (updated in the same task as code changes).

## Required behavior

- For each implemented/changed feature, ensure a matching document exists at `docs/features/<feature-name>.md`.
- If a relevant doc already exists, update it instead of creating a duplicate.
- If the task does not change behavior (pure refactor/chore), briefly confirm whether doc changes are needed.

## Required sections (minimum)

- `# <Feature name>`
- `## Purpose`
- `## Business rules`
- `## Architecture and dependencies`
- `## API/contracts`
- `## Data model and migrations` (or "No schema changes")
- `## Edge cases and known limitations`
- `## How to change safely in future`
- `## Related files`

## Quality constraints

- Be concise and specific; avoid generic descriptions.
- Document invariants, assumptions, and integration boundaries.
- Keep names/path references aligned with actual code.
